# Copy to .env (gitignored — never commit real secret values) and fill in.
# Read by docker-compose.yml's `env_file: .env` on server/worker; resolved
# by packages/cli/src/secrets.ts's real SecretResolver (AMENDMENTS.md A45):
# AART_SECRET_<NAME> env var first, falling back to <root>/secrets.json —
# see DEPLOY.md's "Secret management" section for the full story, including
# the on-disk secrets.json alternative and this approach's real limits (no
# encryption, no rotation, no audit trail beyond the filesystem's own).
#
# <NAME> is whatever you referenced with --webhook-hmac-secret-ref
# secrets.<NAME> (or a bare <NAME>, both are accepted) when running
# `aart trigger add`. Example below matches DEPLOY.md's own walkthrough.
AART_SECRET_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-value

# Add one AART_SECRET_<NAME> line per secret your deployed workflows/
# triggers reference — e.g. an LLM provider key a workflow's llm.* block
# resolves via secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, a GitHub/Slack webhook secret,
# a database credential a custom block resolves through ctx.resolveSecret.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# D1 "remotes + push" (AMENDMENTS.md A56) — a SEPARATE bearer token (NOT an
# AART_SECRET_* ref, a different resolution convention: the plain env var
# name, then <root>/secrets.json's own "AART_DEPLOY_TOKEN" key) gating
# POST /bundles/ingest, POST /bundles/plan, and POST /environments — the
# deploy-surface mutation routes `aart push`/`aart_deploy`/`aart environment
# register --root <remote-store>` (over HTTP) use. Unset -> those three
# routes refuse EVERY request, including a genuinely correct one (fail-
# closed; see DEPLOY.md's "Deploy token" section). Leave unset if you never
# intend to push to this server remotely — every other route is unaffected.
#
# D1 fix pass (AMENDMENTS.md A57) — this SAME var ALSO (conditionally, not
# fail-closed) gates POST /workflows/:id/promote once set, and must be set
# on the DASHBOARD service too (not just server/worker) for its promote
# button to keep working once you set this here — see DEPLOY.md's "Deploy
# token" section's own gating matrix for the full table.
AART_DEPLOY_TOKEN=replace-with-a-different-long-random-value
